
# Thai KIND_PLUR (Phase 8) - limited coverage.
#
# Thai, like Japanese, does not mark plurality morphologically for most
# nouns. Plurality is signalled by reduplication (ๆ) or explicit collective
# markers (ทั้งหลาย, พวก). v1 authors a small set covering the cases where
# Thai DOES mark plurality (reduplication form, classifier-prefixed plural,
# and inherently-collective compounds). Singular kinship (แม่, พ่อ) does NOT
# appear here so it parses via the NP recall path to tell_about.
:KIND_PLUR

# Reduplicated (พหูพจน์) forms
"ลูก ๆ"                 [k child]               .
"เพื่อน ๆ"             [k friend]              .

# Inherently-collective compounds
"พี่ชายและน้องชาย"      [k brother]             .
"พี่สาวและน้องสาว"      [k sister]              .
"พี่น้อง"               [k sibling]             .
"พ่อแม่"               [k parent]              .

# Collective concepts
"ความสนใจ"             interest                .
"ความสัมพันธ์"         [k relationship]        .
